BND-15: do not let the evaporation adjustment make the rate negative

The engine added the monthly [ADJUSTMENTS] EVAPORATION value to the source
rate with no lower bound (climate::updateDailyClimate for constant, monthly
and temperature-based evaporation; SWMMEngine::stepRunoff for time series and
pan evaporation). An adjustment more negative than the source rate gave a
negative rate that added water to subcatchment storage. Stop the rate at zero
once all sources and adjustments are applied, before any API forcing, as the
legacy patch does in setEvap(). Non-negative rates are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-15_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
index 839529d..18a629e 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
@@ -2031,6 +2031,10 @@ void SWMMEngine::stepRunoff(double dt_routing) noexcept {
                 ctx_.climate_state.evap_rate += ctx_.climate_state.adjust_evap[mon];
             }
         }
+        // A negative [ADJUSTMENTS] EVAPORATION value larger than the source
+        // rate stops the rate at zero (legacy setEvap).
+        ctx_.climate_state.evap_rate = std::max(0.0, ctx_.climate_state.evap_rate);
+
         // legacy climate_setState ends by advancing NextEvapDate past the
         // current date (every evaporation type); runoff_getTimeStep then
         // clamps the runoff step so it never crosses it.
